  "synthesis": "First run on Claude Code (sonnet A/B, opus C; 9/9 valid, ~US$2.08). B vs A is flat: outcome 1/3 vs 1/3, compliance 0.67 vs 0.67, tokens -6% and duration equal (noise). B never opened the five added files (all three B runs read the same 5: adapter, worker, bug-fix, fix-root-causes, prove-it-works), so the longer read-first list costs nothing here and also has no effect on a bug fix; the refactoring playbook's benefit needs the planned refactoring case. Failures are one shape in all arms, opus included (C 0/3): price to Decimal, quantity left float, so Decimal*1.5 raises; the judge also fails the two check-passing runs for keeping float math in line_total, which the hidden check misses. Criterion 1 fails in all 9 because the reply graded is the one after the Stop gate, which opens with evidence: a harness artifact, equal across arms. Promote: not worse on any measure."
